`opentelemetry-api`: implement the declarative configuration Instrumentation
Configuration API in `opentelemetry._configuration`, so an instrumentation
library can read its own configuration without depending on the SDK.
Add `ConfigProperties`, a typed read view over the `instrumentation` config node
providing `get_string`/`get_bool`/`get_int`/`get_float`,
`get_config`/`get_config_list`, the typed sequence getters
`get_string_list`/`get_bool_list`/`get_int_list`/`get_float_list`, and `keys`.
Add a global `ConfigProvider` with `get_config_provider`/`set_config_provider`
following the set-once, proxy-default semantics of
`set_tracer_provider`/`get_tracer_provider`, where `get_config_provider` returns
a forwarding `ProxyConfigProvider` until one is set.
In `opentelemetry-configuration`, `configure_sdk` now installs that global
`ConfigProvider`, built from the `instrumentation` config node as the
configuration file wrote it.
